  "description": "<p>This is related to FCREPO-2323: <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2323?focusedCommentId=53282&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-53282\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2323?focusedCommentId=53282&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-53282</a></p>\n\n<p>We use httpd (apache) to reverse proxy tomcat.   This entails adding a value for the proxyName attribute in Tomcat's server.xml config file:</p>\n\n<p>&lt;Connector port=\"8080\" protocol=\"HTTP/1.1\"<br/>\n               connectionTimeout=\"20000\"<br/>\n               proxyName=\"server.artic.edu\"</p>\n\n<p>If I load content via the proxy and link resource 'a' to another ('b'), and then delete the linked resource ('b'), which should remove the relationship from 'a', everything works as expected.  </p>\n\n<p>If, however, I load content using 'localhost:8080,' the link from resource 'a' to resource 'b' remains even after I delete resource 'b'.</p>\n\n<p>The question is whether this is by design (i.e. how tomcat operates when using a proxy) or if it indicates a bug in fcrepo.</p>\n\n<p>Two gists may help to describe the above. Each gist replicates the code used to test this and the resulting output.</p>\n\n<p>The first shows the problem when using 'localhost': <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/kefo/7a8d92ee4e1f7d52639436d299e5a718\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://gist.github.com/kefo/7a8d92ee4e1f7d52639436d299e5a718</a></p>\n\n<p>The second shows the result when using the proxyName:  <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/kefo/d9554f73ce9e47d1975d8b3862242ecf\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://gist.github.com/kefo/d9554f73ce9e47d1975d8b3862242ecf</a></p>\n\n\n",
